{
  "_README": [
    "MANUALLY LABELLED GOLD STANDARD for Phase 10 evaluation.",
    "",
    "Three articles, chosen because they cover the hardest cases in the corpus:",
    "  art_fe7715c7a134 - alias variety + pronoun + nominal coreference",
    "  art_8fc2b35b4aa3 - two similar Russian names, a quote, a paragraph break",
    "  art_5488f6656604 - the Lalit Modi false-merge trap",
    "",
    "SPANS ARE IDENTIFIED BY (sentence, surface, occurrence), NOT by raw character",
    "offsets. Offsets are resolved at load time. This is deliberate: hand-written",
    "character offsets rot the moment preprocessing changes by one character, and a",
    "gold set nobody can maintain is a gold set nobody updates.",
    "",
    "HONEST CAVEAT: these labels were produced by one annotator (the system's own",
    "author), which is the weakest possible annotation setup. Real evaluation needs",
    "at least two independent annotators and an inter-annotator agreement score",
    "(Cohen's kappa) to establish that the task is even well-defined. Where human",
    "annotators disagree, no model can be scored meaningfully. Treat these numbers",
    "as a development signal, not as a published benchmark.",
    "",
    "REVISION 2: the first evaluation run exposed GOLD GAPS -- correct system output scored as false positives purely because the annotation was incomplete (dates, a topic, a country, and all ORG entity links). This is the normal way a gold set is built: you run it, inspect the 'errors', and find that some of them are yours. Numbers before this revision were pessimistic about the system and flattering about the annotation."
